{"term":"individual","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:3919d9b7134bdd5494","definition":"A person considered alone, rather than as belonging to a group of people.","example":"He is an unusual individual.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/individual#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:57be75227a7b87120b","definition":"A single physical human being as a legal subject, as opposed to a legal person such as a corporation.","example":"Every individual is equal before and under the law and has the right to the equal protection and equal benefit of the law without discrimination […].","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/individual#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a0aa809109bdd514c9","definition":"An object, be it a thing or an agent, as contrasted to a class.","example":"It is typically held that chairs, trees, rocks, people and many of the so-called ‘everyday’ objects we encounter can be regarded as individuals.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/individual#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1beec9835fd4bfb888","definition":"An element belonging to a population.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/individual#English","license":"CC-BY